## Third-party components

Wrapp bundles and builds against several third-party components, each under
its own license. These are redistributed as part of the build output and
must have their licenses preserved in any redistribution:

| Component                               | License      | Notes                                   |
|-----------------------------------------|--------------|-----------------------------------------|
| Microsoft.Identity.Client (MSAL.NET, incl. .Broker + .Extensions.Msal) | MIT | NuGet packages         |
| CommunityToolkit.Mvvm                   | MIT          | NuGet package                           |
| MaterialDesignThemes                    | MIT          | NuGet package                           |
| WPF-UI                                  | MIT          | NuGet package                           |
| Microsoft.Web.WebView2                  | Microsoft SDK EULA | NuGet package — allows redistribution |
| Microsoft.PowerShell.SDK                | MIT          | NuGet package                           |
| Markdig.Signed                          | BSD-2-Clause | Transitive dependency of Microsoft.PowerShell.SDK |
| Monaco Editor (vendored under Assets/)  | MIT          | Bundled offline copy                    |
| Git-Windows-Minimal                     | GPL-2.0      | Binaries bundled for git operations     |
| IntuneWin32App (vendored under modules/)| MIT          | MSEndpointMgr community module          |
| PSAppDeployToolkit (vendored under modules/) | LGPL-2.1 | Deployment framework template           |

Downstream redistributors are responsible for complying with each component's
license terms. GPL-2.0 (git) and LGPL-2.1 (PSADT) impose additional obligations
beyond the MIT license of Wrapp itself.
